{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:abd7aa8335a810f7","name":"Intrigue Heroes","source":{"id":"source:reference-abd7aa8335a810f7","title":"Intrigue Heroes","revision":24032,"timestamp":"2024-10-16T15:37:44Z","sha256":"72c9c62d0e5e6367506d957642d2423a2944707c38249ab22b27af878ea7ea3a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24032","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Intrigue%20Heroes&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-abd7aa8335a810f7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars"]}," universe is replete with scenes of breathtaking action, dramatic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," duels, sweeping ship battles, and hair-raising escapes, it is also deeply immersed in intrigue. The galaxy is an enormous place with a huge variety of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", ideologies, corporations, and other groups jockeying to gain power and to carve their own destinies. A dense, if delicate, web of negotiations, treaties, alliances, and obligations weaves disparate groups together to stop the civilizations of the galaxy from descending into chaos. Sometimes this web keeps the peace, but often stability is threatened or overturned as masterminds scheme for more control. For the heroes, adventure is around every corner and, more often than not, comes looking for them instead of the other way around.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaign"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaign"}," has plenty of room for every type of character, although creating heroes for an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaign"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaign"}," requires a bit more thought than it might in other settings. Campaigns that focus on intrigue are less about kicking down doors and tossing thermal detonators (although these is a time and place for that, as well) than about the gradual, but steady, discovery of information and secrets as the heroes unravel plots. This chapter provides more ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"},", and a new twist on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," to help your characters fit into a world of backroom deals, clandestine meetings, blackmail, infiltration, and political maneuvering.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At first glance, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," Heroic Class seems to be the wisest choice in an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaign"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaign"},". To be sure, with its tremendous amount of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," and its intrigue-inspired ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talent Trees"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent_Trees"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," Heroic Class is well suited for this type of campaign, but the other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Classes","referenceId":"reference:3db50eedfbef40fc"}," have just as much to offer. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrels"}," use their silver tongues or dastardly tricks for their own personal gain. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scouts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scouts"},", as masters of infiltration, use their resources to break into government facilities or corporate offices to retrieve valuable information. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers"}," need not be brutish thugs and can include military intelligence officers or bodyguards for the rich and powerful, picking up vital secrets as they go about their duties. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"},", known for their role as peacekeepers and negotiators, find themselves wrapped up in densely woven plots and shifting agendas on a daily basis. In short, every ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Class"}," has its place in an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaign"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaign"},", as long as the characters realize that not every situation can be solved with combat. The heroes must rely on their powers of observation and deduction to move the story along, as well.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Species"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Given the multitude of beings and cultures that inhabit the galaxy, many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," rely on manipulation and diplomacy to advance their causes and do the best for their people. Certain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," use intrigue and social engineering for noble pursuits, such as to maintain pacifist societies. Some, however, excel at pulling the strings of others for the sake of financial or political gain, or merely for the enjoyment of being in control.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SPECIES\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ABILITY MODIFIERS\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["IMAGE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Bith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bith","referenceId":"reference:226574d844698c0d"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Int, +2 Cha, -2 Con\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Defel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defel","referenceId":"reference:80589d956d21b6e7"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Int, -2 Str\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Fosh"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fosh","referenceId":"reference:6f14f8b4ece4d9a6"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Dex, +2 Cha, -2 Con\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Givin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Givin","referenceId":"reference:e4e518b6e7dd6f09"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Int, -2 Str\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Gotal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gotal","referenceId":"reference:5ccb43dbbbd0f713"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["None\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Herglic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Herglic","referenceId":"reference:b9e5a0996259fd4c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+4 Str, -4 Dex\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mrlssi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mrlssi","referenceId":"reference:e535dc07dbcef738"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Int, +2 Cha, -2 Str\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Neimoidian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Neimoidian","referenceId":"reference:907b5a99c5e02624"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Cha, -2 Str\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Umbaran"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Umbaran","referenceId":"reference:71bc927341fdd793"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2 Dex, +2 Wis, -2 Con\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Heroic Classes"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The galaxy is rife with intrigue. Every ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", corporation, planet, fiefdom, and other group has its own agendas and methods for getting its way. With so many interests jockeying for power, for good or for ill, nearly every individual can be considered to be involved in some form of conspiracy, if only as part of a demographic to be catered to or exploited. Even the hinterlands of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"}," are home to plots for riches or power, meaning that only the most isolated creatures can truly pursue their destinies without influence. Heroes, however, are not such beings. They find themselves more enmeshed in the games of intrigue with every passing moment. This section explores how heroes who embrace those schemes and maneuvers can rise to become more than mere pawns- they can be vital parts of the board and, in some cases, the players who move the pieces in the first place.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Noble"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"}," are the movers and shakers of the galaxy, shaping policy, setting examples, and dictating the courses of countless lives. Nobles live and breathe intrigue, from the local level all the way up to the Republic Senate and everything in between. They are masters of brokering deals, shifting attitudes, and shaping mobs to suit a political purpose.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Outside the safety of the palace, corporate boardroom, or Senate, Nobles use their presence and oratorical skills to motivate and their actions to inspire. Most Nobles find violence distasteful, but when a situation turns sour, they are often the first to pick up a blaster to engage in \"extreme negotiations,\" using power to turn the tables. They also know that utter eradication of the enemy is rarely the best solution to a problem. The wisest Nobles use their abilities to persuade their allies as often as they try to win over their opponents.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Nobles realize that the fates of many beings, whether members of their immediate clans or the population of an entire sector, rest on their shoulders. Some Nobles carry this weight with confidence, sacrificing their own best interests for the sake of the people they support. Others see their status and clout as a way to improve their station through graft, corruption, and the general abuse of power. Truly adroit Nobles blur the line between their outward actions and their actual motives. Some act as rakes while attempting to use covert methods to push through important legislation. Others (such as Senator Palpatine) pose as apparently selfless public servants who quietly use their positions to further sinister plots.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaign"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaign"},", Nobles are an obvious choice for a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Class"},". They help soothe frayed feelings and negotiate to gain benefits for their group. They broker deals and diffuse tense situations before blasters are drawn. And Nobles are frequently travelers, using their wealth and influence to dabble in all the limitless experiences of the galaxy, trying new things until they become bored or find something else to draw their attention.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["New Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," are suitable for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," characters within ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaigns"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaigns","referenceId":"reference:a53d5fcc9f89dc26"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["New ",{"tag":"a","children":["Master of Intrigue Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Master_of_Intrigue_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:7df077580570cb24"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["New ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:7042cd72401e10bc"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["New ",{"tag":"a","children":["Superior Skills Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Superior_Skills_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:e4795623e8afa68f"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Scoundrel"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Like ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrels"}," thrive in the maze of obligations, corruption, and deals that runs throughout so much of the galaxy. Perhaps better than most, they understand how intrigue is part of the fabric of society and view it as a resource to be exploited rather than reviled. Successful Scoundrels can use the web of pacts, lies, and compromises to their advantage, pitting opposing groups against each other or finding holes in the system that they can exploit for political, personal, or financial gain.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although the general impression of Scoundrels is that they live and work in the margins of society, just as many cruise the upper echelons of the galaxy, wheeling and dealing with Senators, HoloNet stars, prominent business people, and other elite individuals. This arena of intrigue is ripe with opportunity for Scoundrels to run con jobs and commit outright theft. However, those who dare to rise to this level of society are playing a dangerous game- beings of privilege and influence usually play for keeps, and it takes just one wrong word or deal gone bad for them to crush the offender. Sometimes this retribution comes through legal channels, but more often than not, the elite dispatch private bodyguards or bounty hunters to exact revenge for lost revenue, fouled business agreements, or failed political ventures.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Of course, just as some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"}," fail to live up to their name, some Scoundrels fail to live down to theirs. More than a few revolutions are led by charismatic, talented Scoundrels who use clandestine activities or guerilla tactics to win freedom from oppression. For these Scoundrels, the system is broken, and they consider it futile to attempt routine diplomacy or work through the courts. They know that only grand gestures- in the form of bombs, hacked HoloNet feeds, or kidnappings of prominent individuals- will grab the attention of uncaring leaders and the docile masses.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["New Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," are suitable for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," characters within ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaigns"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaigns","referenceId":"reference:a53d5fcc9f89dc26"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["New ",{"tag":"a","children":["Revolutionary Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Revolutionary_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:f0d1846a3941889e"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Scout"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Intelligence gathering is vital for any sort of clandestine activity, legal or otherwise. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scouts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scouts"}," serve as forward observers, reconnaissance experts, advanced deployment personnel, and explorers for all manner of organizations. Although Scouts might believe that their travels to the far-flung regions of the galaxy keep them free from the entanglements of intrigue, most would be alarmed to find that they still are used as cogs in the machine of conspiracy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Not all Scouts are silent stalkers; some are scientists and researchers who prefer doing their experiments in the field for immediate results. In this pursuit, they might become embroiled in the politics of their university, corporation, or patron. New discoveries might be fast-tracked before they are ready to be revealed or quietly hushed up to avoid disrupting markets or upsetting the status quo. The discovery of an ancient Sith ruin or an unknown cache of prized ore is precious knowledge- knowledge that can be exploited by the right group. Scouts who reveal this information to the public for the good of all might find themselves the targets of greedy or angry forces that want such secrets for their own reasons.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Scouts also serve the vital role of exploring unknown regions, mapping new areas of space and being the first to encounter unfamiliar ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," and civilizations. In any first-contact scenario, Scouts serve as impromptu ambassadors, deciding what information to share with (and conceal from) new acquaintances. Although most of these Scouts are not as skilled at diplomacy as are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"},", they must try to reach friendly accords with the newly discovered people- if only to escape with their skins intact. On occasion, primitive ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," might mistake Scouts for gods or demons and petition them to answer questions or resolve disputes. Unscrupulous Scouts take advantage of this confusion to enrich themselves or carve out their own small fiefdoms to exploit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["New Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," are suitable for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," characters within ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaigns"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaigns","referenceId":"reference:a53d5fcc9f89dc26"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["New ",{"tag":"a","children":["Espionage Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Espionage_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:6c7265cfe45aef25"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Soldier"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers"}," serve as pawns in the intricate plots of various organizations in the galaxy. When negotiations break down or when force seems to be the most logical way to further an agenda, Soldiers serve on the front lines, using their might to advance the edicts of a distant individual or group that sits safely behind durasteel walls and powerful shields. For Soldiers, the circumstances do not matter- they receive their orders (or promises of pay) and do their duty to the best of their ability.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although many Soldiers relish the relatively simple life of combat, their job is to serve the interests of others. Thus, even the most combat-oriented Soldiers can find themselves part of elaborate plans, bureaucratic entanglements, or the like. Some Soldiers begin to question the motives or rationale behind a particular engagement or the faction they serve. A few turn traitor or reinterpret their orders to their own liking, often at the risk of reprisal. Soldiers with an entrepreneurial spirit might follow their orders to the letter but dabble in their own projects on the side, using the chaos of war to benefit themselves in some way. Although no professional army admits it, graft and corruption are always present, and war profiteering lines the pockets of those willing to seize the initiative. Company quartermasters sell \"lost or destroyed\" equipment, intelligence officers purchase bonds or strike deals based on their secret findings, and so on.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In times of conflict, Soldiers might be the only ones willing and able to deal with the locals and, as a result, could be dragged into all manner of schemes and obligations, some of which might seem beyond their capabilities. For example, Soldiers might be asked to help rebuild villages or negotiate peace between opposing groups; while doing so brings the Soldiers short-term benefits, the long-term consequences could embroil them in intrigue and politics outside the scope of their field manual's guidelines.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["New Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," are suitable for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," characters within ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intrigue Campaigns"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intrigue_Campaigns","referenceId":"reference:a53d5fcc9f89dc26"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["New Talents: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Brawler Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brawler_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:a4c88f1c0d979625"},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Crowd Control"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crowd_Control"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Disarm and Engage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarm_and_Engage"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Entangler"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Entangler"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reverse Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reverse_Strength"}]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["New Talents: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commando Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commando_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:1ccfc7af27121192"},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Coordinated Effort"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coordinated_Effort"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dedicated Guardian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dedicated_Guardian"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dedicated Protector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dedicated_Protector"}]}]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Prestige Classes"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," expand the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talent Trees"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent_Trees"}," available to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prestige Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prestige_Classes"}," in the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Ace Pilot"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Nobles, Senators, captains of industry, and other VIPs rely on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ace Pilots"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ace_Pilots"}," to operate their luxurious ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," and to deliver them to their destinations in one piece. These talented pilots are experts at using defensive flying maneuvers to keep their ships, and the riders within, safe from harm.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["New Talents: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Expert Pilot Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Expert_Pilot_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:b20ca56fa02b22aa"},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Clip"],"href":"https://swse.mir